# ── MARK LV — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# Git has no trailing comments: text after a pattern becomes part of it, so
# every comment here sits on its own line above the pattern it describes.

# Your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/api_keys.json
# The dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# A LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp
# account, not just a key
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
# Google OAuth client secrets
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
# SQLite's write-ahead log and shared memory next to memory.db
memory/*.db-*
# The old memory file, kept after it was moved into memory.db
memory/*.bak
# Your contacts: names and phone numbers of the people you write to and call
config/contacts.json

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Wake-word models downloaded from the settings panel (tens of MB)
config/wake_models/
# The embedding model for memory search (1.24 GB, downloaded on first start)
config/embed_models/
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
